WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.351
The continuous water blancher moves cut strips
through a simulated residence zone.

00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:09.107
Belt travel provides evidence of the time spent
in that zone.

00:00:09.317 --> 00:00:15.831
Connect the blancher belt encoder to AI05, and
the conveyor speed output to AO05.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:19.447
A requested speed and observed travel are
different signals.

00:00:19.657 --> 00:00:22.769
Set the model residence time to 90 seconds.

00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:26.015
Check the accepted window before testing the
transfer.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.354
Inject the stale encoder fault.

00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:33.409
A retained speed value is insufficient when new
encoder evidence stops arriving.

00:00:33.619 --> 00:00:37.854
Restore the encoder and verify travel time with
a simulated marker.

00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:42.632
In the worked balance, added water makes output
mass greater than input mass.
